# README Template

## Project number/title

- **Authors:** Your name and your group members' names
- **Group name:** Your group name

## Overview

Concisely explain what the program does. If this exceeds a couple of
sentences, it may be too long. Generally, use the project specification as a
guide, but paraphrase it rather than copying it.

## Manifest

List the source files and other non-generated files, with a brief, one-line
explanation of the purpose of each file.

## Building the project

Explain how to build your code. If you are delivering a library, say where it
needs to be installed and how to use it. If this is an executable, explain
how to get started quickly.

## Features and usage

Summarise the main features of your program and explain how to use it.

## Testing

Describe how you tested your code in enough detail to show the tests that
were performed and what they verified.

## Known bugs

List known bugs that you were unable to fix.

## Reflection and self-assessment

Discuss the issues you encountered during development and testing. What
problems did you have? What did you need to research and learn on your own?
What errors did you encounter, and how did you fix them?

What parts of the project did you find challenging? Did anything finally
"click" as you worked on the project? How well did development and testing go?

## Sources used

List any sources you used outside the textbook. Cite websites, documentation,
and AI assistance where applicable.
